+# Experimental iOS 18 host
+
+Target for this work: standard iPhone 15 (A16), iOS 18.7.7. This is an
+uncompiled development patch, not a playable port or an IPA. No Dynasty
+Warriors game binary, shader, asset, region or version has been examined.
+
+## Scope
+
+The opt-in `DM_IOS_M3=1` path uses ordinary Metal render/compute/blit command
+encoders, direct resource binding and `useResource` declarations for indirect
+argument-buffer references. Main, upload, segmented and present submissions
+use the ordinary command queue. The existing Metal 4 path remains the default.
+The shader translation chain and all seven game profiles are unchanged.
+
+The API adaptation is derived from d2r-mobile's MIT-licensed commit
+[`d9e95c3`](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/d2r-mobile/commit/d9e95c33812faaf58ddedf53772c8d0b43c9a685).
+It is adapted to nxnative's newer copy ordering, segmented submissions,
+magenta diagnostics and scaled/format-changing texture copies. The buffer
+address registry grows dynamically and validates complete index-buffer ranges;
+it has no fixed 512-buffer limit. Registration is non-owning, protected by the
+existing lock, and removed with residency retirement.
+
+The build variant targets iOS 18.0 with an A14 CPU baseline (usable by A16).
+It still needs a real Apple SDK build and signing for installation. Merely
+lowering the deployment target is insufficient; the actual encoder APIs,
+submission completion, synchronization and presentation paths differ.
+
+## Checks without any game content
+
+From the repository root, on a host with Python, `cpp` and a C compiler:
+
+```sh
+python3 dm/ios/tests/test_ios18_port.py
+```
+
+This runs six test methods: project generation/error handling, legacy source
+preprocessing for iPhone/simulator/Mac, delimiter checks, and the C address
+registry under AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. The registry test
+covers 4,096 buffers, boundary/overflow/duplicate/removal cases and 100,000
+operations checked against a separate model. Preprocessing strips unavailable
+system headers, so it does **not** validate Objective-C API declarations.
+
+In a container where LeakSanitizer cannot inspect `/proc`, run the same command
+with `ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0`. Bounds/use-after-free and undefined-behavior
+instrumentation remain active; leak detection is not validated in that run.
+On Windows without a C compiler/preprocessor, those checks are reported skipped.
+
+On a Mac with Xcode, the next asset-free check is:
+
+```sh
+GAME=010015100B514000 bash dm/ios/tools/check_m3_apple.sh
+```
+
+The existing profile supplies compile-time constants only; it does not supply
+game code or assets. This checks the two graphics translation units, including
+their headers and included implementation fragments, against the real iPhoneOS
+SDK with iOS 18 availability errors enabled. It does not link the whole host,
+install, or exercise the GPU. Repeat with other profiles as appropriate.
+
+## Build after game-specific preparation
+
+When a supported game's rewritten modules, RomFS and iOS shader libraries have
+already been produced in its work folder:
+
+```sh
+DM_IOS_M3=1 GAME=<existing-profile-id> W=<game-work-folder> \
+  bash dm/ios/tools/build_ipa.sh <output.ipa>
+```
+
+The front-end NSP script inherits `DM_IOS_M3=1` too. An unrecognized game still
+only produces a survey; this change does not bypass that restriction. The
+temporary legacy project spec is removed on exit. Builds remain unsigned.
+
+## Remaining gates
+
+1. Run the Apple SDK check, link the host and validate an unsigned IPA's minimum
+   OS and CPU load commands. None has run in the Linux development environment.
+2. Exercise the backend's synthetic rendering/upload/readback tests on Apple
+   hardware, then install a diagnostic build on the target iPhone. Validate
+   presentation, completion order, app suspension and memory pressure.
+3. Survey the player's own Dynasty Warriors 9 Empires / 真・三國無双8 Empires
+   game files. Identify region, version, module Build IDs, SDK, imports, shader
+   containers and actual texture formats. Add a real profile from that evidence.
+4. Validate game startup, menus, combat, audio, controls, saves, memory, thermals
+   and sustained frame pacing on iPhone 15 / iOS 18.7.7.
+
+The standard iPhone 15 has no hardware BC texture support. Existing generic
+BC decoding paths remain available, but the game's actual format mix and the
+cost of decoding/expanded textures are unknown. D2R's game-specific ASTC pack
+is not a drop-in asset solution for this title. Do not infer playable performance
+or memory fit from API compatibility checks.
